@chapter Protocol

The @strong{usawa} project does not specify a strict protocol.

However, to guide the implementation to fulfill the design goals, some recommendations are given in the following.


@section Publishing and dissemination

All parties that wish to follow the ledger must be given clear rules on how to receive new entries.

There should be more than one channel through which entries are published, and ideally these "channels" should also include different platforms.


@subsection Dissemination example

All participants could be asked to follow both a @strong{nostr}@footnote{nostr is an ownerless, client- and server-agnostic protocol for publishing arbitrary content ("notes and other stuff"): @url{https://nostr.com/}} and an @emph{email mailist list}, that both would publish the full entry data as clearly defined data structures. 

Also, all participants would be encouraged to follow an @emph{EVM chain}@footnote{A list of EVM chains: @url{https://chainlist.org/}} that could publish the latest ledger state digest in the data field of a transaction.


